{
  "title": "Marketplace and Classifieds: Let Other People Sell on Your Site | CrestApps for Orchard Core",
  "description": "A site can do more than sell its own products. With the CrestApps Marketplace, other sellers, called vendors, list products while your store takes the payment, keeps a commission and pays them once the sale is safe from returns. With Classifieds, your visitors post their own listings, such as ads, directory entries or homes for sale, and you approve them before they show.\n\nIn this video:\n• Why open your site to other sellers, and how both modules are organized\n• Marketplace settings: commission, days held, and payouts\n• Adding a vendor, and choosing it on a product\n• A vendor's sales, what is held, ready and paid out, and releasing a sale\n• What the people who run a vendor see in their account\n• Letting visitors post a kind of listing\n• Posting, approving, rejecting, renewing and upgrading listings\n• Searching listings by words and distance\n• Use cases",
